{%- comment -%}
  SUPERSEDED 25 Aug 2026 — DO NOT EDIT, AND DO NOT DELETE YET.

  This one section carried all five elements of the skate page, which meant
  reordering them or dropping one for a week was a Liquid edit. It has been
  split into `aj-grind-hero`, `aj-grind-categories`, `aj-grind-mission`,
  `aj-grind-featured` and `aj-grind-foot`, and `templates/page.grind.json` now
  assembles those. The categories gained an image per tile in the move, which is
  what prompted it.

  IT STAYS ON DISK UNTIL THE NEW PAGE IS CONFIRMED LIVE. A theme push and the
  GitHub sync are not one atomic step, and a template pointing at a section type
  the theme does not have renders nothing at all. Deleting this file is the last
  move, not the first. Its preset is removed so it cannot be added to anything
  new in the meantime.

  The styles it used to carry now live in `assets/aj-grind.css`, shared by all
  five. This file's own `{% stylesheet %}` block is left intact so that it still
  renders correctly if anything is still pointing at it.

  ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

  YOINK SKATE SHOP — a skate shop inside The Yoink. v2.

  THE FILE IS STILL CALLED aj-grind. The page was drafted as "The Grind" and
  renamed on 17 Aug 2026; the section TYPE is what `templates/page.*.json` binds
  to, so renaming the file orphans the live page for the sake of a filename. The
  brand lives in the settings, where it belongs.

  INDEPENDENT, NOT NEARBY. The argument is not "buy local to you" — a customer in
  Mesa is not closer to any of these shops than to a warehouse. It is that the
  money goes to an independent skate shop rather than to a distributor. Copy on
  this page should never imply proximity, because that promise would be false
  for almost every reader.

  THE PRODUCTS ARE THE STORY, NOT THE SHOPS. v1 named the shops under the hero.
  Alex's call on 17 Aug 2026 was to sell their products without advertising them,
  so that band is now a mission statement carrying the same argument with no
  names in it — see the note above it. There is still NO DEAL here: every other
  surface on this store sells on price, and a discount would bury the one thing
  that makes this page worth existing.

  THE ERA WITHOUT THE MARKS. Tony Hawk, THPS, Powell Peralta and Element are all
  live trademarks and this is a commercial page. What is free is the GRAMMAR of
  1999 skate media: griptape black, a video-game HUD, warped display type, spray
  stencils, VHS grain. The categories are laid out as selectable levels because
  that is the device everyone remembers, and it costs nothing to borrow.

  FIVE LEVELS, SIX SLOTS. The loop skips any slot with no name, so the count is
  a content decision rather than a layout one. The five are the store's own
  tags — YLSD, YLSTW, YLSH, YLSSG, YLSA — each behind a smart collection of its
  own, all five children of `skate-local` (tag YLSS, 334 products).

  IT DEGRADES TO NOTHING GRACEFULLY. The product row checks its collection first
  and the category tiles link out whether or not a collection exists behind
  them. A v1 that only renders when the catalogue is finished is a v1 nobody can
  look at. Worth knowing: an API-created collection is published to NOTHING by
  default, so a tile can point at a real collection and still 404. All five were
  published explicitly to the same seven channels as the parent.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign s = section.settings
-%}

<div class="aj-grind" style="{% render 'spacing-style', settings: section.settings %}">

  {%- comment -%} ---- hero ---- {%- endcomment -%}
  <div class="aj-grind__hero">
    <div class="aj-grind__tape" aria-hidden="true"></div>

    <div class="page-width aj-grind__hero-inner">
      <p class="aj-grind__kicker">{{ s.kicker | escape }}</p>

      {%- comment -%}
        THE MARK, WHEN THERE IS ONE. The hero is griptape black, so a logo here
        has to read light-on-dark — a dark PNG disappears completely and the page
        looks broken rather than unbranded.

        The heading is not dropped when a logo is present, it is kept as the
        accessible name and hidden visually. A shop whose name exists only inside
        a PNG has no name as far as search or a screen reader is concerned.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- if s.logo != blank -%}
        <img
          class="aj-grind__logo"
          src="{{ s.logo | image_url: width: 900 }}"
          alt="{{ s.heading | escape }}"
          width="{{ s.logo.width }}"
          height="{{ s.logo.height }}"
          style="--aj-grind-logo-w: {{ s.logo_width }}px;"
          loading="eager"
        >
        <h1 class="aj-grind__title visually-hidden">{{ s.heading | escape }}</h1>
      {%- else -%}
        <h1 class="aj-grind__title">{{ s.heading | escape }}</h1>
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- if s.subheading != blank -%}
        <p class="aj-grind__sub">{{ s.subheading | escape }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- comment -%}
        THE HUD. A score counter is the one piece of 90s skate furniture that
        can carry real information — so it does: what the shop is, not a number
        invented to look busy.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <ul class="aj-grind__hud" role="list">
        <li><span class="aj-grind__hud-k">Shops</span><span class="aj-grind__hud-v">{{ s.hud_shops | escape }}</span></li>
        <li><span class="aj-grind__hud-k">Orders</span><span class="aj-grind__hud-v">{{ s.hud_deal | escape }}</span></li>
        <li><span class="aj-grind__hud-k">Shipping</span><span class="aj-grind__hud-v">{{ s.hud_ships | escape }}</span></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>

  {%- comment -%}
    ---- the mission ----

    THIS BAND USED TO NAME THE SHOPS, AND DELIBERATELY NO LONGER DOES. Alex's
    call, 17 Aug 2026: sell their products, do not advertise them. Listing the
    suppliers by name sends a reader off to buy direct, and it also writes a
    promise this page then has to keep — the moment a named shop stops stocking,
    the band is a lie until someone remembers to edit it.

    So what is left is the argument itself, which is true whoever is stocking it
    and needs no maintenance. The `shop` block type is gone with the list; if
    named shops ever come back they should come back as real data, not as three
    text fields somebody has to keep in step.

    Gated on the statement rather than on blocks, so the band is present exactly
    when there is something to say.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if s.mission_body != blank -%}
    <div class="aj-grind__shops-band">
      <div class="page-width aj-grind__section">
        <p class="aj-grind__eyebrow aj-grind__eyebrow--on-dark">{{ s.mission_eyebrow | escape }}</p>
        <h2 class="aj-grind__h2 aj-grind__h2--on-dark">{{ s.mission_heading | escape }}</h2>
        <p class="aj-grind__shops-body">{{ s.mission_body | escape }}</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- comment -%} ---- the categories, as levels ---- {%- endcomment -%}
  <div class="page-width aj-grind__section">
    <p class="aj-grind__eyebrow">{{ s.cats_eyebrow | escape }}</p>
    <h2 class="aj-grind__h2">{{ s.cats_heading | escape }}</h2>

    <ul class="aj-grind__levels" role="list">
      {%- for i in (1..6) -%}
        {%- liquid
          assign nkey = 'cat_' | append: i | append: '_name'
          assign hkey = 'cat_' | append: i | append: '_handle'
          assign bkey = 'cat_' | append: i | append: '_blurb'
          assign name = s[nkey]
          assign handle = s[hkey]
          assign blurb = s[bkey]
        -%}
        {%- if name != blank -%}
          <li class="aj-grind__level">
            <a href="{% if handle != blank %}{{ routes.all_products_collection_url | replace: '/collections/all', '/collections/' | append: handle }}{% else %}#{% endif %}">
              <span class="aj-grind__level-no">{{ forloop.index | prepend: '0' | slice: -2, 2 }}</span>
              <span class="aj-grind__level-name">{{ name | escape }}</span>
              {%- if blurb != blank -%}<span class="aj-grind__level-blurb">{{ blurb | escape }}</span>{%- endif -%}
              <span class="aj-grind__level-go">Drop in &rarr;</span>
            </a>
          </li>
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endfor -%}
    </ul>
  </div>

  {%- comment -%}
    ---- a product row, only when there is something in it ----
    Same rule the merch shelf follows: a shelf advertising an empty collection
    is worse than one fewer row.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- liquid
    assign featured = collections[s.featured_handle]
  -%}
  {%- if featured != blank and featured.products.size > 0 -%}
    <div class="page-width aj-grind__section">
      <p class="aj-grind__eyebrow">{{ s.featured_eyebrow | escape }}</p>
      <h2 class="aj-grind__h2">{{ s.featured_heading | escape }}</h2>
      <ul class="aj-grind__grid" role="list">
        {%- for product in featured.products limit: 4 -%}
          {%- assign v = product.selected_or_first_available_variant -%}
          <li class="aj-grind__card">
            <a href="{{ product.url }}">
              <span class="aj-grind__shot">
                {%- if product.featured_image -%}
                  <img src="{{ product.featured_image | image_url: width: 600 }}"
                       alt="{{ product.featured_image.alt | escape }}"
                       width="300" height="300" loading="lazy">
                {%- endif -%}
              </span>
              <span class="aj-grind__card-name">{{ product.title | escape }}</span>
              <span class="aj-grind__card-price">{{ v.price | money }}</span>
            </a>
          </li>
        {%- endfor -%}
      </ul>
    </div>
  {%- endif -%}

  <div class="page-width aj-grind__section aj-grind__foot">
    <p class="aj-grind__foot-line">{{ s.foot_line | escape }}</p>
    {%- if s.cta_text != blank and s.cta_link != blank -%}
      <a class="aj-grind__cta" href="{{ s.cta_link }}">{{ s.cta_text | escape }}</a>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
</div>

{% stylesheet %}
  /*
    GRIPTAPE IS THE GROUND. The whole page sits on near-black with a grit
    texture, which is the one surface every skater has looked at for hours. The
    brand's purple and yellow ride on top of it rather than under it — this is
    the only Yoink surface that is not built on white or purple, and it should
    feel like a different room in the same building.
  */
  /*
    NO `section` CLASS ON THE ROOT, and this is the second time this codebase has
    paid for the lesson. Adding it to pick up the theme's width handling let the
    theme win `background` on that element — the black ground vanished, `color:
    #fff` still applied, and the page shipped white on white with only the
    purple text-shadow visible. `aj-join` carries the same warning from 7 Aug.

    Background and text colour stay together on a class this file owns and
    nothing else targets, and the gutter is handled below rather than borrowed.
  */
  .aj-grind {
    background: #0f0f11;
    color: #ffffff;
  }

  /*
    THE SECTION OWNS ITS OWN GUTTER. `.page-width` computed to max-width: none
    and zero padding inside this template — the theme's rule keys off a chain
    this page does not reproduce, so content sat flush against both viewport
    edges at 1920 and would have touched the text on a phone. Constraining it
    here means the page cannot depend on where it is mounted, which is the whole
    point of a landing page that will move.
  */
  .aj-grind .page-width {
    max-width: var(--page-width, 87.5rem);
    margin-inline: auto;
    padding-inline: clamp(1.25rem, 5vw, 3.5rem);
  }

  .aj-grind__hero { position: relative; padding: clamp(3rem, 9vw, 6rem) 0 clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3.5rem); overflow: hidden; }

  /* The grit: two offset dot fields, which reads as griptape and costs nothing
     to ship. A photograph of grip would be a 400KB texture doing the same job. */
  .aj-grind__tape {
    position: absolute; inset: 0; pointer-events: none; opacity: 0.55;
    background-image:
      radial-gradient(rgba(255,255,255,0.10) 1px, transparent 1px),
      radial-gradient(rgba(255,255,255,0.07) 1px, transparent 1px);
    background-size: 5px 5px, 7px 7px;
    background-position: 0 0, 3px 4px;
  }

  .aj-grind__hero-inner { position: relative; }

  .aj-grind__kicker {
    font-family: "Ohpixel", var(--font-heading--family);
    text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    font-size: clamp(0.75rem, 1.6vw, 0.9rem);
    color: var(--aj-brand-yellow, #ffe000);
    margin: 0 0 0.9rem;
  }

  .aj-grind__title {
    font-family: "Flashy", var(--font-heading--family);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: clamp(3.5rem, 13vw, 9rem);
    line-height: 0.88;
    margin: 0;
    color: #fff;
    /* A hard offset shadow in brand purple: the cheapest way to make display
       type read as a sticker rather than as a heading. */
    text-shadow: 0.06em 0.06em 0 var(--aj-brand-purple, #7a3fa0);
  }

  /* The supplied mark, standing in for the display type. Width is the setting
     and height follows, so a logo of any proportion keeps its own shape rather
     than being squashed into a box the theme picked. */
  .aj-grind__logo {
    display: block;
    width: min(var(--aj-grind-logo-w, 320px), 100%);
    height: auto;
  }

  .aj-grind__sub {
    margin: 1.4rem 0 0; max-width: 46ch;
    font-size: clamp(1rem, 2.4vw, 1.25rem); line-height: 1.45;
    color: rgb(255 255 255 / 0.86);
  }

  /* ---- the HUD ---- */
  .aj-grind__hud {
    display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.75rem;
    margin: 2rem 0 0; padding: 0; list-style: none;
  }
  .aj-grind__hud li {
    display: grid; gap: 0.15rem;
    padding: 0.6rem 1rem;
    background: rgb(255 255 255 / 0.06);
    border: 1px solid rgb(255 255 255 / 0.14);
    border-radius: 4px;
  }
  .aj-grind__hud-k {
    font-family: "Ohpixel", monospace; text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em; font-size: 0.7rem; color: var(--aj-brand-cyan, #5cd8f8);
  }
  .aj-grind__hud-v { font-weight: 700; font-size: 0.95rem; }

  /* ---- sections ---- */
  .aj-grind__section { padding: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 4rem) 0; }

  .aj-grind__eyebrow {
    font-family: "Ohpixel", var(--font-heading--family);
    text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    font-size: 0.8125rem; color: var(--aj-brand-cyan, #5cd8f8);
    margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
  }
  .aj-grind__eyebrow--on-dark { color: var(--aj-brand-yellow, #ffe000); }

  .aj-grind__h2 {
    font-family: "Flashy", var(--font-heading--family);
    font-weight: 400; font-size: clamp(2rem, 5.5vw, 3.25rem);
    line-height: 1; margin: 0 0 1.6rem; color: #fff;
  }

  /* ---- the levels ---- */
  .aj-grind__levels {
    display: grid; gap: 0.9rem; margin: 0; padding: 0; list-style: none;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
  }
  @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
    .aj-grind__levels { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); }
  }

  .aj-grind__level a {
    display: grid; gap: 0.35rem; height: 100%;
    padding: 1.25rem 1.25rem 1.1rem;
    background: #17171b;
    border: 1px solid rgb(255 255 255 / 0.12);
    border-left: 4px solid var(--aj-brand-yellow, #ffe000);
    border-radius: 6px;
    text-decoration: none; color: #fff;
    transition: transform 0.12s ease, background 0.12s ease;
  }
  .aj-grind__level a:hover { transform: translateY(-2px); background: #1e1e24; }

  .aj-grind__level-no {
    font-family: "Ohpixel", monospace; font-size: 0.75rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em; color: rgb(255 255 255 / 0.45);
  }
  .aj-grind__level-name {
    font-family: "Flashy", var(--font-heading--family);
    font-weight: 400; font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 4vw, 2.1rem); line-height: 1;
  }
  .aj-grind__level-blurb { font-size: 0.95rem; color: rgb(255 255 255 / 0.7); line-height: 1.4; }
  .aj-grind__level-go {
    margin-top: auto; padding-top: 0.5rem;
    font-family: "Ohpixel", monospace; text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em; font-size: 0.75rem; color: var(--aj-brand-yellow, #ffe000);
  }

  /* ---- the mission band ----
     Class names kept as __shops-* because the live template and any saved
     section settings still reference this block by them; renaming CSS to match
     new copy is not worth a repaint of markup that is working. */
  .aj-grind__shops-band { background: var(--aj-brand-purple, #7a3fa0); }
  .aj-grind__shops-body { margin: 0; max-width: 52ch; line-height: 1.5; color: rgb(255 255 255 / 0.92); }

  /* ---- featured products ---- */
  .aj-grind__grid { display: grid; gap: 1rem; margin: 0; padding: 0; list-style: none; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); }
  @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
    .aj-grind__grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr); }
  }
  .aj-grind__card a { display: grid; gap: 0.4rem; text-decoration: none; color: #fff; }
  .aj-grind__shot {
    display: block; aspect-ratio: 1 / 1; overflow: hidden;
    border-radius: 6px; background: #1a1a1f;
  }
  .aj-grind__shot img { width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: cover; display: block; }
  .aj-grind__card-name { font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.3; }
  .aj-grind__card-price {
    font-family: "Flashy", var(--font-heading--family);
    font-size: 1.25rem; color: var(--aj-brand-yellow, #ffe000);
  }

  /* ---- foot ---- */
  .aj-grind__foot { text-align: center; }
  .aj-grind__foot-line {
    font-family: "Flashy", var(--font-heading--family);
    font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 2.25rem); line-height: 1.1;
    margin: 0 0 1.4rem; color: #fff;
  }
  .aj-grind__cta {
    display: inline-block; padding: 0.95rem 1.8rem;
    background: var(--aj-brand-yellow, #ffe000);
    color: var(--aj-brand-ink, #282828);
    border-radius: 6px; font-weight: 800; text-decoration: none;
  }
  .aj-grind__cta:hover { filter: brightness(1.06); }
{% endstylesheet %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "AJ Yoink Skate Shop",
  "tag": "section",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "header", "content": "Hero" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "kicker", "label": "Kicker", "default": "A skate shop inside The Yoink" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "heading", "label": "Heading", "default": "Yoink Skate Shop" },
    { "type": "image_picker", "id": "logo", "label": "Logo",
      "info": "The hero is near-black, so this has to read light-on-dark — a dark mark disappears entirely. The heading stays as the accessible name whether or not a logo is set." },
    { "type": "range", "id": "logo_width", "label": "Logo width", "min": 120, "max": 560, "step": 20, "unit": "px", "default": 320 },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "subheading", "label": "Subheading",
      "default": "Decks, trucks, hardware and safety gear from independent skate shops — and a bit of our own. Same gear, one checkout." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "hud_shops", "label": "HUD — shops", "default": "Independent, not chains" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "hud_deal", "label": "HUD — second stat", "default": "Every order goes back" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "hud_ships", "label": "HUD — third stat", "default": "Ships from the shop" },

    { "type": "header", "content": "Categories",
      "info": "Five squares are filled. A square with no name renders nothing, so the sixth is the slot to use if another category is ever tagged." },
    { "type": "paragraph", "content": "The sixth slot has NO default keys. Shopify rejects the whole file with \"default can't be blank\" if a text setting carries default: \"\" — omit the key instead. theme check does not catch it and the GitHub sync drops the file in silence." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "cats_eyebrow", "label": "Eyebrow", "default": "Pick your line" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "cats_heading", "label": "Heading", "default": "Five ways in" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "cat_1_name", "label": "1 name", "default": "Decks" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "cat_1_handle", "label": "1 collection handle", "default": "skate-decks" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "cat_1_blurb", "label": "1 blurb", "default": "Blanks, pros and shop boards." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "cat_2_name", "label": "2 name", "default": "Trucks & Wheels" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "cat_2_handle", "label": "2 collection handle", "default": "skate-trucks-wheels" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "cat_2_blurb", "label": "2 blurb", "default": "The bits that grind and the bits that roll." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "cat_3_name", "label": "3 name", "default": "Hardware" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "cat_3_handle", "label": "3 collection handle", "default": "skate-hardware" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "cat_3_blurb", "label": "3 blurb", "default": "Bearings, bolts, bushings, griptape, stickers." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "cat_4_name", "label": "4 name", "default": "Safety Gear" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "cat_4_handle", "label": "4 collection handle", "default": "skate-safety-gear" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "cat_4_blurb", "label": "4 blurb", "default": "Helmets and pads. No lecture." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "cat_5_name", "label": "5 name", "default": "Apparel" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "cat_5_handle", "label": "5 collection handle", "default": "skate-apparel" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "cat_5_blurb", "label": "5 blurb", "default": "Shoes, tees and hats." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "cat_6_name", "label": "6 name" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "cat_6_handle", "label": "6 collection handle" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "cat_6_blurb", "label": "6 blurb" },

    { "type": "header", "content": "Mission",
      "info": "Deliberately does not name the shops — see the note in the file. Clearing the statement removes the whole band." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "mission_eyebrow", "label": "Eyebrow", "default": "Why this exists" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "mission_heading", "label": "Heading", "default": "Bought from a shop, not a warehouse" },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "mission_body", "label": "Statement",
      "default": "Skate shops are independent, outnumbered and closing. Everything here is stocked by one of them, so the money goes to people who have stood on a board rather than to a distributor who has not." },

    { "type": "header", "content": "Featured row" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "featured_eyebrow", "label": "Eyebrow", "default": "On the shelf" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "featured_heading", "label": "Heading", "default": "In the shop now" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "featured_handle", "label": "Collection handle",
      "info": "Renders nothing until this collection has products, so the page is safe to ship before the suppliers are onboarded.",
      "default": "skate-local" },

    { "type": "header", "content": "Foot" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "foot_line", "label": "Line", "default": "Same deck. Bought from a skate shop instead of a warehouse." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "cta_text", "label": "Button", "default": "Meet the shops" },
    { "type": "url", "id": "cta_link", "label": "Button link" },

    { "type": "header", "content": "Spacing" },
    { "type": "range", "id": "padding-block-start", "label": "Top padding", "min": 0, "max": 100, "step": 4, "unit": "px", "default": 0 },
    { "type": "range", "id": "padding-block-end", "label": "Bottom padding", "min": 0, "max": 100, "step": 4, "unit": "px", "default": 0 }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
